{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":162,"timestamp":"2026-07-22T17:03:48.807537Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2538c31c-31fb-429e-b6e4-02dac0721c93","title":"l2r1 minor collector: shell trust posture and diagnostics","description":"(1) security: glob match fail-open on overlapping prefix/suffix (substrate.rs:89). (2) security: tilde expansion trusts HOME and mis-falls-back to repo-root when HOME unset, turning ~/ entries into misleading absent-artifact failures (substrate.rs:117-118) — SE converges. (3) security: chassis stdout flows unsanitized into terminal-destined display fields (acquire.rs:93). (4) security+SE: the git failure Diagnostic ships empty recovery members and a hardcoded token against the vocabulary discipline, renders an empty machine-form file field, and leaks absolute paths via message — the #730 clause applies to refs.rs's Diagnostic construction (refs.rs:95,100). (5) security: PATH-resolution trust posture undeclared for both subprocess sites — state it (a malicious crosslink/git on PATH is the operator's environment, likely out of model — but say so). (6) security nit: binding-failure detail embeds both absolute roots in Status-destined prose (substrate.rs:47) — the #730 clause. (7) QE: local_refs origin-stripping/HEAD-filter/dedup has no test. Owner: security/software-engineer. Validator: solution-architect.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"a5f3c2ee-ad1f-47f3-a24e-a04dfa4ce652","created_by":"xqjG"},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQACsVyW+vier9XcuT6yaVLbkTfHTIZTR58LXGFIddNkIu2udkxwPURZOCUK5kgErnf2MrHi+U5qXwLBYjw90+gE="}
